# Tauri 2 desktop (Infinity Express)

## Stack

- Shell is **Tauri 2** (not Electron). Frontend is Vite + React under `src/`.
- Rust entry: [`src-tauri/src/lib.rs`](src-tauri/src/lib.rs) via `app_lib::run()`.
- Scripts: `npm run tauri:dev` / `tauri:build`. Browser-only: `npm run dev`.

## Plugins in use

Registered on the builder in `lib.rs`:

- `tauri-plugin-dialog` → `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog`
- `tauri-plugin-fs` → `@tauri-apps/plugin-fs`

NPM also has `@tauri-apps/api` (e.g. `isTauri()`).

Capabilities: [`src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`](src-tauri/capabilities/default.json)

- `core:default`
- `dialog:default` (open + save)
- `fs:allow-write-text-file`
- `allow-list-subdir-names` / `allow-remove-mod-dir` (app commands in [`permissions/mod-fs.toml`](src-tauri/permissions/mod-fs.toml))

Dialog-selected paths are **auto-scoped for the session**, so `writeTextFile` on a path returned by `save()` does not need a broad FS allow-list. Scope is not persisted across app restarts. Arbitrary user paths (mods download dir) use custom Rust `std::fs` commands instead of plugin-fs scopes.

## Frontend helpers

Prefer extending [`src/lib/desktop/`](src/lib/desktop/) over scattering plugin imports:

| Helper | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `isDesktopApp()` | `isTauri()` from `@tauri-apps/api/core` |
| `saveTextFile(name, contents)` | `save({ defaultPath, filters })` then `writeTextFile`; `false` if cancelled |
| `pickDirectory(title?)` | `open({ directory: true, multiple: false })`; `null` if cancelled or not Tauri |
| `listSubdirNames(path)` | invoke `list_subdir_names`; `[]` if not desktop / empty path |
| `removeModDir(downloadDir, folderName)` | invoke `remove_mod_dir` (case-insensitive folder match under download dir); no-op if not desktop |

### Call sites

- **Export Save** ([`ExportDialog.tsx`](src/ui/ExportDialog.tsx)): desktop → `saveTextFile`; browser → `downloadText` Blob fallback.
- **Engine / Settings Browse** ([`EngineStation.tsx`](src/ui/EngineStation.tsx), [`SettingsDialog.tsx`](src/ui/SettingsDialog.tsx)): `DirectoryField` → `pickDirectory`; game paths via [`gameFolderPrefs.ts`](src/lib/ui/gameFolderPrefs.ts); app dirs via [`appDirPrefs.ts`](src/lib/ui/appDirPrefs.ts).
- **Mods disk presence / remove** ([`useUserCatalog.ts`](src/hooks/useUserCatalog.ts)): scan download dir; Download ID = folder name; remove deletes that folder.

## Prefs vs native storage

Plain string prefs (game folders, chrome, detail pane, mods catalog) use **localStorage** helpers under `src/lib/ui/` (and `userCatalog`). Do **not** add `tauri-plugin-store` unless persistence must live outside the webview.

## Adding more native FS

1. Cargo + npm plugin (if new), **or** app `#[tauri::command]` + `std::fs` for arbitrary user paths.
2. `.plugin(...::init())` and/or `invoke_handler` in `lib.rs`.
3. Capability permission in `default.json` (and `permissions/*.toml` for app commands).
4. Thin wrapper in `src/lib/desktop/`; keep browser fallbacks when useful.

